  "measurement_notes": [
    "Real inference on one Windows computer, one operator account, one CPU resource domain and one admission slot. Three signed agent identities do not establish independent providers.",
    "The six elapsed_ms observations include request completion, settled-session inspection and a deliberate 1250 ms counter wait. These are acceptance durations, not throughput or WAN benchmarks.",
    "Concurrent-call counter deltas overlap and are not attributed billing meters. Loaded counters include model discovery, weights and earlier accepted work since process boot.",
    "The three detection_ms values measure time to the terminal/refunded session observation after fault injection, not Windows process-kill latency or a recovery SLO. Hard-crash resolution took about 35 seconds.",
    "Forced supervisor and guardian termination leave the last diagnostic phase READY; current process-aware status reports not running/live. The terminated processes cannot publish a final phase.",
    "All five affected contributor processes were gone and all owned TCP/UDP ports were free after each fault. The sibling remained alive. Whole-route model reload restored actual inference after each fault.",
    "The native guardian is a locally built, SHA-256-pinned Windows executable. Job containment covers ordinary CreateProcess descendants; it is not OS account isolation, a hostile-engine sandbox, root/coordinator lifecycle protection or CPU/RAM/GPU resource caps.",
    "No second computer, new model download, fabricated receipt, client cancellation, changed operator identity or extra LAB_GRANT was used. Private input/output text and private keys are excluded.",
    "Public check labels summarize the three concrete fault records; the original private report reused a generic mid_execution_quic_loss label for all failures. Measured values and historical evidence were not changed."
